      "The serving decision is provisional until the A and B owners agree this fallback (docs/contract-semantics.md) and a temporal holdout is possible."
    ],
    "b05_limitations": [
      "The split is NOT chronological (one-date scrape), so coverage is measured on a random duplicate-group-isolated sample of the same period. Future listings will be drawn from a shifted market and real coverage can be lower. Re-calibrate on a chronological split.",
      "Intervals describe the ASKING price of listings, not what tenants finally pay.",
      "Coverage is a marginal average over served rows under exchangeability of calibration and serving rows. It is not a guarantee for any single listing, district or price level; see conditional_coverage for the observed spread.",
      "Calibration reuses the validation split that B04 used for CatBoost early stopping, so validation residuals can be slightly optimistic; compare test_to_validation_median_ae_ratio.",
      "Reposts and identical units in one building were merged for splitting, but listings from the same tower can still sit in calibration and test, which makes in-sample coverage optimistic.",
      "Intervals are withheld for coordinate-only requests, areas outside the training range and sparse locations; they are not calibrated for those cases and must not be replaced by an observed standard deviation.",
      "Blanking optional inputs keeps the same quantile, but the true error grows; see scenarios.missing_features for the coverage drop before relying on sparse requests.",
      "Width is large relative to price because rents are noisy given the available features (no renovation or building-type data); the provisional width target is reported, not met by tuning."
    ],
